<h3>H. Non-Solicitation</h3><p>During the engagement and for twelve (12) months thereafter, the Client shall not, directly or indirectly, solicit or employ any personnel or vendor of the Company engaged in providing the Services, without the Company''s prior written consent.</p>
<h3>I. Assignment &amp; Subcontracting</h3><p>The Company may subcontract or engage vendors to perform the Services. The Client shall not assign or transfer its rights or obligations without the Company''s prior written consent.</p>
<h3>J. Notices</h3><p>Notices may be given in writing to the address or email provided in the onboarding application (for the Client) or the Registered Office / grievance email above (for the Company); electronic notices shall be deemed validly served.</p>
<h3>K. Limitation of Claims</h3><p>Any claim arising out of or in connection with the engagement must be notified in writing within six (6) months of the event giving rise to it, failing which the claim shall be deemed waived, to the extent permitted by law.</p>
<h3>L. Dispute Resolution &amp; Amendments</h3><p>The parties shall first attempt to resolve any dispute amicably and in good faith. Failing resolution, the dispute shall be referred to arbitration by a sole arbitrator under the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996, seated at Rajahmundry, Andhra Pradesh, conducted in English; the courts at Rajahmundry shall have jurisdiction for interim relief. These Terms, together with the applicable work order / agreement, constitute the entire agreement and may be amended only in writing.</p>

<h3>M. Site, Statutory Approvals &amp; Equipment (Hospital Projects)</h3><p>The Client shall ensure site readiness, access, utilities and safe working conditions, and shall obtain and maintain all statutory approvals and licences applicable to the healthcare establishment and its equipment (including fire, pollution, building, AERB / radiation, drug and clinical-establishment approvals as relevant). Medical equipment and materials are supplied subject to manufacturer / supplier specifications, availability and lead times; warranties are those of the manufacturer and are passed through to the Client; title and risk in goods pass to the Client on delivery. Costs arising from unforeseen site conditions, statutory changes or price escalation (including material and GST rate changes) shall be to the Client''s account.</p>
', version = '2026-08-05-v2', content_hash = 'onb-hospital-projects-2026-08-05-v2', is_active = true
where division_code = 'hospital-projects' and is_active = true;

